  "answer": "This has been reported before. The Copilot key doesn't show up under \"Remap a key\" because Windows sends it as a shortcut: Win (Left) + Shift (Left) + F23. To remap it, open Keyboard Manager and choose \"Remap a shortcut\". Click the pencil icon, press the Copilot key, and pick your target key or shortcut. This works for mapping to letters or other keys. Mapping it to Ctrl is unreliable: the key can behave as Ctrl+Shift, and it can stop working after Windows updates. Some users say they got Win + Shift + F23 → Ctrl (Left) to work. A standalone \"Remap a key\" entry for the Copilot key is still only a feature request. Those tickets are the place to follow it."
 },
